Two reds, 28 seconds apart, two different tree hashes.

`runRed`'s hashRepo (packages/commands/src/lifecycle.ts:490-501) computes
sourceTreeHash(repoDir, [<studio rel>, ".bisellium", ...manifest.source_excludes],
"HEAD"), and sourceTreeHash reads `git ls-tree -r HEAD` — a pure function of the
HEAD *commit*. It cannot move because the working tree was edited. So two reds
on the same HEAD must carry the same hash.

Both reds ran on the same HEAD. Proof from the logs' own bodies, which print
live sourceTreeHash values for the repo under test:
  01.log: withoutSlash = ba2380fcd3b2c14277c993f719dcbb4e3d95f012
          noExclusions = de35874a49b6628e1cde3341f070682a2dd427fa
